---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii3_72",
  "series": "Band II 3 (1695 - 1700)",
  "seq": 72,
  "text": "<p> [[191.4]] <b>72. LEIBNIZ AN MICHEL ANGELO FARDELLA</p>\n<p> [[191.5]] Hannover, 3./13. September 1696. [71.77.]</b></p>\n\n<p> [[191.18]] Vir celeberrime, Fautor et Amice Honorande. </p>\n<p> [[191.19]] Gratias <Fn><i>Am Kopf der Seite von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Dn. Mich. Angelo Fardellae Professori Patavino 3/13 September 1696.</Fn> ago quod Ongarelli meministi, aliorumque quae desiderabam circa Vergeriana et\n[[191.20]] monasterium Carcerum. Salisburgi relicta spero ad nos delatum iri interventu amici Augustani. </p>\n<p> [[192.1]] Perplacent etiam quae de opere tuo mox prodituro memorantur in Scheda quam misisti,\n[[192.2]] cui titulus est <i>Galleria di Minerva parte 2.</i> An hoc forte est quasi quoddam diarium eruditorum;\n[[192.3]] quo librorum editorum vel edendorum contenta explicantur? </p>\n<p> [[192.4]] Verissimum est multa praeclara contineri in Augustino etiam ad philosophiam theologiae\n[[192.5]] cognatam illustrandam, et operae pretium esse facturum qui dispersa per ejus scripta, in unum\n[[192.6]] colligat. Et cum Platonica non minus quam Aristotelica ei fuerint explorata, et illa magis etiam\n[[192.7]] amata, Plato autem ad veritatem Theologiae naturalis multo Aristotele propius accesserit, eo\n[[192.8]] uberiores poterunt fructus percipi ex Augustino. Interim fatendum est, haec tantum (ut sic\n[[192.9]] dicam) Incunabula esse veritatis, quam meo judicio ad majorem longe maturitatem jam perducere\n[[192.10]] datur, idque Tibi non potest non esse exploratum, tum ex iis quae coram locuti sumus,\n[[192.11]] tum etiam ex iis quae literis subinde inter nos commutatis continentur; et ex iisdem multo\n[[192.12]] adhuc plura elicere aliquando licebit credoque mea principia sic esse comparata, ut etiam apud\n[[192.13]] vestros tuto allegari possint; nam et in Gallia placuere viris doctis Romanae partis; neque adeo\n[[192.14]] indigne ferent vestri si meas quasdam sententias Tibi probari significes, tametsi hominis\n[[192.15]] ultramontani. </p>\n<p> [[192.16]] Augustinum puto Pythagoreae et Platonicae scholae placita secutum. Nam per Pythagoram\n[[192.17]] inprimis de Mentis immaterialitate et immortalitate dogma ex oriente allatum in Graecia\n[[192.18]] inclaruit. Plato autem longius progressus vidit, non alias vere substantias esse quam Animas,\n[[192.19]] corpora autem in perpetuo fluxu versari. Cogitata horum emendavit atque etiam auxit Augustinus\n[[192.20]] ad normam christianae sapientiae, hunc Scholastici, sed longo intervallo, sunt secuti. Mihi\n[[192.21]] summa rei videtur consistere in vera Notione substantiae, quae eadem est cum notione Monadis,\n[[192.22]] sive realis Unitatis et ut ita dicam Atomi Formalis; vel puncti essentialis, nam materialis\n[[192.23]] Atomus dari non potest, unde frustra in materia quaeritur Unitas, et punctum Mathematicum\n[[192.24]] non est essentiale sed modale, unde continuum ex punctis non constat, et tamen quicquid\n[[193.1]] substantiale est ex unitatibus conflatur. Haec considerans majore jam fructu veterum meditationibus\n[[193.2]] poterit uti, velut clave naturae superioris reperta quam scholastici nimia modalitatum\n[[193.3]] cura neglecta substantia; recentiores nimio materialium id est collectitiorum studio, ignorata\n[[193.4]] Monade, obscurarunt: Hanc doctrinam spero a Te posse illustrari, et magnam lucem addi meis\n[[193.5]] qualibuscunque philosophematis, quemadmodum et Mathematica sive Analytica mea reperta a\n[[193.6]] Domino Marchione Hospitalio Parisiis et a Dominis fratribus Bernoulliis, quorum alter Basileae\n[[193.7]] alter jam Groningae Matheseos professorem agit, mire sunt promota. Et nunc Dn. Marchio\n[[193.8]] Hospitalius (qui R.P. Malebranchii amicus est singularis) de nova mea methodo calculi differentialis\n[[193.9]] vel infinitesimalis (infinitesimalia enim seu infinite parva ut ordinariorum differentias\n[[193.10]] vel incrementa momentanea considero, et ita calculo subjicio) libellum peculiarem edidit,\n[[193.11]] ingenuitate laudabili professus, qualiacunque mea has interiores Matheseos fores sibi aperuisse.\n[[193.12]] Quia igitur aliquam Analyseos meae notitiam petis, ideo hunc libellum suadeo ut ex Gallia Tibi\n[[193.13]] afferri cures et lectionem eorum adjungas speciminum novi calculi mei quae in Actis Lipsiensibus\n[[193.14]] vel a Bernoulliis vel a me edita habentur. Ita Tibi non difficile erit pro eo quo vales\n[[193.15]] ingenio in haec mysteria penetrare. Nam magnum inprimis usum habet calculus ille in transferenda\n[[193.16]] Mathesi ad naturam, quia de infinito ratiocinari docet, omnia autem in natura habent\n[[193.17]] characterem infiniti autoris. Unde ipse Hugenius paulo ante mortem cum hoc calculandi genus\n[[193.18]] sibi familiare reddidisset et usurpare coepisset, agnovit, partim in <i>Actis eruditorum</i> partim in\n[[194.1]] suis ad me literis, posse ita detegi ad quae alias vix admitteremur. Quod si aliquando Florentiam\n[[194.2]] excurrere vacabit, multa poterit Tibi explicare Dominus Baro de Bodenhausen amicus\n[[194.3]] Domini Magliabecchii et meus, qui et ipse his est mysteriis initiatus, donec aliquando nobis\n[[194.4]] iterum colloqui detur, quod suavissimum utrique fore auguror. Fortasse non inutile erit ut\n[[194.5]] nonnihil in praefatione operis Tui attingas de nostra hac Analysi infiniti, ex intimo philosophiae\n[[194.6]] fonte derivata, qua Mathesis ipsa ultra hactenus consuetas notiones id est ultra imaginabilia\n[[194.7]] sese attollit, quibus pene solis hactenus Geometria et Analysis immergebantur. Et haec nova\n[[194.8]] inventa Mathematica partim lucem accipient a nostris philosophematibus, partim rursus ipsis\n[[194.9]] autoritatem dabunt. </p>\n<p> [[194.10]] Quae de foecunditate animae habentur in transmissa scheda minus intelligo. Mihi omnis\n[[194.11]] substantia operationum mire fertilis videtur. Sed a substantia (praeterquam infinita) substantiam\n[[194.12]] id est Monada produci non arbitror. In quo puto nos non dissensuros, si mutuo intelligamur.\n[[194.13]] Vale etc. </p>\n<p> [[194.14]] P. S. Qui corporis Essentiam in extensione consistere dicunt (de quibus quaeris) rem non\n[[194.15]] satis explicant. Extensionis notio non est primitiva, ut Cartesiani sibi persuadent, sed composita\n[[194.16]] et supponit alterius rei repetitionem. Hinc nullum quidem datur vacuum, non sufficit tamen\n[[194.17]] extensio ad corpus intelligendum. Spatium et tempus non sunt substantiae sed relationes reales. </p>\n<p> [[194.18]] (: Praeterita <Fn>(: Praeterita ... ipsa. :): <i>Diesen Satz hat Leibniz in eckige Klammern gesetzt, wohl um ihn von der Abfertigung auszuschließen.</i></Fn> scilicet in praesentibus exprimuntur, unde realis est relatio praesentium ad\n[[194.19]] ipsa. :) Itaque eorum sententia qui dicunt spatium esse corpus in genere mihi non satisfacit.\n[[194.20]] Quid (quaeso) dicent esse tempus an motum in genere? Sed neutrum meo judicio dici debet. </p>\n",
  "number": "72.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN MICHEL ANGELO FARDELLA",
  "date": "Hannover, 3./13. September 1696. [71.77.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:72. LEIBNIZ AN MICHEL ANGELO FARDELLA Hannover, 3./13. September 1696. [71.77.] Vir celeberrime, Fautor et Amice Honorande. Gratias Am Kopf der Seite von Leibniz' Hand: Dn. Mich. Angelo Fardellae Professori Patavino 3/13 September 1696. ago quod Ongarelli meministi, aliorumque quae desiderabam circa...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>